SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Vrysiani (Nativity of the Virgin)\, Exambela
LOCATION:Exambela\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 17th-century Moni Vrysis below Exambela\, with its small ecclesiastical museum\, celebrates the Nativity of the Virgin with vespers and a monastery-table panigiri on the evening of 7 September — chickpea soup\, lamb\, wine and a takimi in the courtyard. It's a ten-minute walk down from Exambela village\; a good one to combine with a September stay in Apollonia when the island has calmed down.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#exambela-panigiri-of-panagia-vrysiani-nativity-of-the-virgin
